course: dictionary
lesson: 15270
title: Signatory: the one who signs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A signatory is a person, group or country that has signed an official agreement. Look for the clue hidden inside the word: sign. «The signatories agreed to protect the rainforest.» The people who signed the agreement are the signatories.
explain: A signatory can also be a country. «Many countries are signatories to the human rights treaty.» This means these countries have signed the treaty and agreed to follow it. Signatory can also work as an adjective, as in «signatory countries».
explain: When you meet a hard word, check your idea by putting it into the sentence. Try «signed» in place of signatories: «The countries that signed the treaty agreed to protect the rainforest.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A signatory is a person, group or country that has signed an official agreement, contract or treaty.
fact: «Signatory» can be a noun (a signatory, signatories) or an adjective (signatory).
fact: On a bank account, a signatory is a person allowed to sign cheques and approve payments.
fact: «Authorised signatory» means someone officially allowed to sign for a person or group.
fact: The word «sign» is hidden inside «signatory», which is a clue to its meaning.
exercise: «The signatories to the treaty met in Geneva.» Who are the signatories? | The people who wrote the weather report | The tourists visiting Geneva | *The countries and people who signed the treaty | The children who read the treaty aloud
exercise: A bank account needs an authorised signatory. What does a signatory do on a bank account? | *Signs cheques and approves payments | Looks after the cash in the till | Counts the coins in the machine | Opens the windows of the bank
exercise: What word is hidden inside signatory? | stay | *sign | slip | sing
test: «Many countries are signatories to the agreement.» What does signatories mean here? | Countries that are cancelling their holidays | *Countries that have signed the agreement | Countries that are drawing the map | Countries that have never heard of the agreement
test: A signatory on a bank account can do what? | *Sign cheques | Walk the dog | Sleep in the vault | Paint the office walls
exam: Why do the signatories of a treaty sign it? | *To show they agree to follow it | To stop the meeting | To make the paper heavier | To win a prize
